# Quantitative worker runtime dependencies.
#
# These MUST stay in lockstep with the direct dependency versions pinned in
# pyproject.toml's [project.dependencies] -- that pin is what the committed
# reports under reports/ were generated against, and drifting it here would be
# a silent statistical change. Bump both together, never one alone.
#
# Deliberately excludes streamlit/plotly/pyarrow (the interactive lab's `app`
# extra): the worker never renders a UI, so those ~300MB of transitive
# dependencies do not belong in a worker execution image (architecture plan
# Section 11.3, "slim the image").
#
# This is the scientific stack for the whole xtra_takehome core (matplotlib
# for report figures, yfinance for data fetching) -- both genuinely needed by
# `python -m xtra_takehome` and its own tests. The Phase-2 worker CONTAINER
# specifically builds from requirements/worker-image.lock instead (see that
# file's own header comment): a strict subset of this file, pinned to the
# same versions, that additionally excludes yfinance/matplotlib because
# neither is reachable from anything the worker process actually imports.
arch==7.2.0
matplotlib==3.10.3
numpy==2.2.6
pandas==2.2.3
scipy==1.15.3
statsmodels==0.14.4
yfinance==0.2.61
